# Tailwind for New UI

Style every new component, page, and feature with Tailwind utility classes on `className`. This app uses Tailwind v4 (`@import "tailwindcss"` in `src/index.css`, `@tailwindcss/vite` in `vite.config.ts`).

Do not add CSS modules, styled-components, Emotion, Sass, new `.css` files, `<style>` tags, or inline `style={{ ... }}` for layout or visuals. Keep `src/index.css` as the Tailwind entry (`@import "tailwindcss"` only) unless a global `@theme` token is required.

## Patterns

Match existing Finley UI: `slate` neutrals, `indigo` for active/focus, `emerald` for positive amounts, `rose` for negative change. Prefer layout utilities (`flex`, `grid`, `gap-*`) and shared card chrome (`rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-sm`).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — inline styles or custom CSS
<div style={{ padding: 20, background: "#fff" }}>Balance</div>

// ❌ BAD — new stylesheet
import "./StatCard.css";

// ✅ GOOD — Tailwind utilities
<div className="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
  <span className="text-sm font-medium text-slate-500">Balance</span>
  <div className="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold">$4,280.00</div>
  <div className="mt-1 text-xs font-medium text-emerald-600">+3.2%</div>
</div>
```

Conditional styles: concatenate utility strings (or `` className={`... ${cond ? "text-emerald-600" : "text-rose-500"}`} ``), not separate CSS classes. Extract repeated class strings into a shared component rather than a new CSS file.
